This product includes software developed as part of the ARCLUX project.

This product includes patterns and algorithms adapted from the following
MIT-licensed open source projects:

- madge (https://github.com/pahen/madge) — Copyright (c) 2017 Patrik Henningsson
  Used as reference for circular dependency detection algorithm.

- git-truck (https://github.com/git-truck/git-truck) — Copyright (c) 2022 git-truck
  Used as reference for graph interaction UX patterns.

- opencode (https://github.com/sst/opencode) — Copyright (c) 2025 opencode
  Used as reference for theme tokens and filtered-list pattern.

Full license texts for the above projects are MIT License, available at
their respective repositories.

- webpro-nl/knip (https://github.com/webpro-nl/knip) — MIT License
  Traversal strategy (import-graph walk + re-export chain following)
  referenced for detectUnusedExports.ts. Re-implemented against ARCLUX's
  own ModuleInfo/ResolvedImport types, not a direct port.

- pacocoursey/cmdk (https://github.com/pacocoursey/cmdk) — MIT License
  Used directly as a dependency (see apps/web/package.json) for
  CommandPalette.tsx's keyboard navigation and accessibility primitives.
  The fuzzy-match scoring algorithm in packages/search/fuzzyScore.ts is
  separately adapted (re-typed to TypeScript, renamed) from this project's
  src/command-score.ts.

- forever (https://github.com/foreverjs/forever) — MIT License
  Read for reference on cross-process state visibility (getAllProcesses/
  getSockets pattern: scan a directory of per-process records, verify
  liveness before trusting a record, self-clean stale entries). ARCLUX's
  packages/storage/SnapshotManager.ts re-implements this concept using
  plain JSON files + process.kill(pid, 0) liveness checks instead of
  forever's UNIX-socket-based IPC — no code copied, pattern only.
